      "README.md": "# Bill-of-Materials & Social Graph Reachability Engine\n\n## Architectural Overview\n\nA fixed-point recursive CTE execution engine supporting working-table iteration, UNION vs UNION ALL deduplication, path-array cycle detection, Bill-of-Materials cost rollup, and NULL-safe NOT EXISTS anti-joins.\n\nIn production relational and analytical database systems—spanning PostgreSQL, SQLite, MySQL/InnoDB, and DuckDB—understanding how query clauses, schema constraints, index structures, and storage engines execute under the hood separates surface-level query authors from staff-level database engineers. This capstone build lab guides you through implementing **Bill-of-Materials & Social Graph Reachability Engine** from first principles with deterministic self-test invariants.\n\n## Guided Implementation Walkthrough (4 Progressive Steps)\n\n### Step 1: Fixed-Point WITH RECURSIVE Iterator with Cycle Detection\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Anchor Member + Iterative Working Table Expansion with Visited Path Array\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`RecursiveGraphEngine.traverseHierarchy`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `traverseHierarchy(edges, rootId, maxDepth)` using SQL `WITH RECURSIVE` working-table semantics. Track `path: [...parent.path, childId]` on every tuple and skip any edge where `parent.path.includes(childId)` to prevent infinite recursion on cyclic graphs.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Seed working table with anchor nodes; in each step expand children where !node.path.includes(childId).`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 1\n\n### Step 2: Bill-of-Materials (BOM) Multiplicative Quantity & Cost Rollup\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Propagating Component Quantities Down Assembly Trees\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`RecursiveGraphEngine.computeBomCost`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `computeBomCost(bomEdges, unitCosts, rootPartId)` to recursively expand sub-assemblies, multiplying component quantities along each root-to-leaf path and summing total unit costs.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Multiply parent.extendedQty * edge.qty down the hierarchy and sum leaf unit_cost * extendedQty.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 2\n\n### Step 3: NULL-Safe NOT EXISTS Anti-Join vs NOT IN Trap\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Why NOT EXISTS Succeeds When Subquery Output Contains NULL\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`RecursiveGraphEngine.notExistsAntiJoin`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `notExistsAntiJoin(outerRows, innerRows, key)` so that `null` values in `innerRows` never poison the anti-join result (unlike `NOT IN`).\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Return outer rows where !innerRows.some(inRow => inRow[key] !== null && inRow[key] === outRow[key]).`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 3\n\n### Step 4: Correlated LATERAL Top-K Per Parent Node\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Evaluating a Parameterized Subquery Per Outer Tuple (CROSS APPLY)\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`RecursiveGraphEngine.lateralTopK`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `lateralTopK(parents, children, fkCol, metricCol, k)` to execute a correlated top-$k$ subquery for each parent row.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `For each parent row, filter childRows matching parent.id, sort descending by metricCol, and take k.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 4\n\n## Relational & Storage Engine Guarantees\n\n- **Curriculum Domain**: Subqueries, CTEs & Recursion\n- **Difficulty & Time Budget**: Advanced (~40 minutes)\n- **Key Architectural Highlights**:\n  - Fixed-point iterative working-table evaluation matching SQL WITH RECURSIVE semantics\n  - Path-vector cycle detection preventing infinite loops on cyclic dependency graphs\n  - Bill-of-Materials component multiplication and NULL-safe NOT EXISTS anti-join evaluation\n- **Core Primitives & Tags**: `Recursive CTE`, `Graph Traversal`, `Cycle Detection`, `Bill of Materials`, `NOT EXISTS`\n\n## Related Curriculum Units\n\n- [scalar row table subqueries](/topic/scalar-row-table-subqueries/)\n- [correlated subqueries mechanics](/topic/correlated-subqueries-mechanics/)\n- [exists not exists null safety](/topic/exists-not-exists-null-safety/)\n- [lateral joins cross apply](/topic/lateral-joins-cross-apply/)\n- [common table expressions with](/topic/common-table-expressions-with/)\n\n## Production Database Context & Verification\n\nThis from-scratch relational engine component is engineered with zero external dependencies and deterministic verification harnesses. Every internal database invariant—from three-valued logic (`TRUE` / `FALSE` / `UNKNOWN`), referential integrity, and fan-out-free join pre-aggregation to B+Tree page splits, MVCC snapshot visibility (`xmin` / `xmax`), slotted-page compaction, and ARIES write-ahead log crash recovery—is asserted directly in `test.js`. Use the interactive browser workbench above to complete the 4 guided steps in **Guided Lab** mode or inspect and benchmark the complete reference architecture in **Full Solution** mode.\n"
