      "README.md": "# Normalize a Legacy Flat Spreadsheet into a 3NF/BCNF System\n\n## Architectural Overview\n\nAn algorithmic functional dependency analyzer implementing Armstrong’s Axiom attribute closure X+, candidate key discovery, BCNF violation detection, and lossless-join decomposition.\n\nIn production relational and analytical database systems—spanning PostgreSQL, SQLite, MySQL/InnoDB, and DuckDB—understanding how query clauses, schema constraints, index structures, and storage engines execute under the hood separates surface-level query authors from staff-level database engineers. This capstone build lab guides you through implementing **Normalize a Legacy Flat Spreadsheet into a 3NF/BCNF System** from first principles with deterministic self-test invariants.\n\n## Guided Implementation Walkthrough (4 Progressive Steps)\n\n### Step 1: Attribute Closure (X+) via Armstrong’s Reflexivity & Transitivity\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Fixed-Point Expansion of Determined Attributes\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`NormalizationEngine.attributeClosure`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `attributeClosure(attrs, fds)` to compute the attribute closure $X^+$ of an attribute set `attrs` under a set of functional dependencies `fds = [{ left: [...], right: [...] }]`.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Repeatedly add fd.right attributes into closure whenever every attribute in fd.left is already in closure.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 1\n\n### Step 2: Superkey & Candidate Key Verification\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Testing Whether X+ Covers All Relation Attributes R\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`NormalizationEngine.isSuperkey`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `isSuperkey(allAttrs, candidateAttrs, fds)` by testing whether the attribute closure of `candidateAttrs` equals the universal attribute set `allAttrs`.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Compute attributeClosure(candidateAttrs, fds) and check if every attribute of allAttrs is present.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 2\n\n### Step 3: BCNF Violation Detector\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Identifying Non-Trivial FDs X -> Y Where X Is Not a Superkey\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`NormalizationEngine.findBcnfViolations`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `findBcnfViolations(allAttrs, fds)` to return every non-trivial functional dependency $X \\to Y$ whose determinant $X$ is not a superkey of `allAttrs`.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `For each FD, filter out right attributes already in left; if remaining right is non-empty and !isSuperkey(allAttrs, fd.left, fds), record violation.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 3\n\n### Step 4: Lossless-Join BCNF Decomposition & Flat-Row Projection\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Splitting R Into R1 = X+ and R2 = (R - (X+ - X)) Without Spurious Tuples\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`NormalizationEngine.decomposeBcnfStep`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `decomposeBcnfStep(allAttrs, violatingFd, fds)` to perform one lossless-join BCNF split into `{ r1, r2 }` and project a flat spreadsheet dataset into deduplicated normalized relations.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Compute closure = attributeClosure(violatingFd.left, fds); R1 = closure, R2 = allAttrs minus (closure - violatingFd.left).`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 4\n\n## Relational & Storage Engine Guarantees\n\n- **Curriculum Domain**: Relational Schema Design & Normalization\n- **Difficulty & Time Budget**: Advanced (~40 minutes)\n- **Key Architectural Highlights**:\n  - Attribute closure X+ fixed-point computation via Armstrong’s Axioms\n  - Minimal superkey / candidate key synthesis over arbitrary functional dependency sets\n  - Automated BCNF violation detector and lossless-join relation decomposition\n- **Core Primitives & Tags**: `Functional Dependencies`, `Attribute Closure`, `3NF & BCNF`, `Lossless Decomposition`, `Normalization`\n\n## Related Curriculum Units\n\n- [entity relationship modeling](/topic/entity-relationship-modeling/)\n- [functional dependencies keys](/topic/functional-dependencies-keys/)\n- [first normal form atomicity](/topic/first-normal-form-atomicity/)\n- [second third normal form](/topic/second-third-normal-form/)\n- [boyce codd fourth fifth normal form](/topic/boyce-codd-fourth-fifth-normal-form/)\n\n## Production Database Context & Verification\n\nThis from-scratch relational engine component is engineered with zero external dependencies and deterministic verification harnesses. Every internal database invariant—from three-valued logic (`TRUE` / `FALSE` / `UNKNOWN`), referential integrity, and fan-out-free join pre-aggregation to B+Tree page splits, MVCC snapshot visibility (`xmin` / `xmax`), slotted-page compaction, and ARIES write-ahead log crash recovery—is asserted directly in `test.js`. Use the interactive browser workbench above to complete the 4 guided steps in **Guided Lab** mode or inspect and benchmark the complete reference architecture in **Full Solution** mode.\n"
