      "README.md": "# Interactive EXPLAIN Plan Bottleneck Detector & Query Rewriter\n\n## Architectural Overview\n\nA cost-based EXPLAIN ANALYZE plan tree analyzer that computes cardinality estimation Q-Error, flags external disk sorts and high-filter sequential scans, and rewrites non-sargable SQL predicates.\n\nIn production relational and analytical database systems—spanning PostgreSQL, SQLite, MySQL/InnoDB, and DuckDB—understanding how query clauses, schema constraints, index structures, and storage engines execute under the hood separates surface-level query authors from staff-level database engineers. This capstone build lab guides you through implementing **Interactive EXPLAIN Plan Bottleneck Detector & Query Rewriter** from first principles with deterministic self-test invariants.\n\n## Guided Implementation Walkthrough (4 Progressive Steps)\n\n### Step 1: Cardinality Estimation Q-Error Calculator\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Measuring Multiplicative Optimizer Estimation Error: max(est/act, act/est)\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`ExplainPlanAnalyzer.computeQError`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `computeQError(estimatedRows, actualRows)` to compute the symmetric multiplicative Q-Error used in query optimizer research.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Clamp est and act to at least 1 to avoid division by zero, then return Math.max(e / a, a / e).`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 1\n\n### Step 2: Buffer Pool & Disk Page Cost Estimator\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: System R / PostgreSQL Weighted Page + Tuple CPU Cost Formula\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`ExplainPlanAnalyzer.estimateScanCost`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `estimateScanCost({ seqPages, tuples, selectivity, seqPageCost, randomPageCost, cpuTupleCost })` to compute both `seqCost` and `indexCost` and choose the cheaper access path.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `seqCost = seqPages * seqPageCost + tuples * cpuTupleCost; idxCost = randPages * randomPageCost + matchedTuples * cpuTupleCost.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 2\n\n### Step 3: Recursive EXPLAIN ANALYZE Bottleneck Detector\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Walking Plan Trees to Flag High-Filter Seq Scans, Disk Spills, and Severe Q-Error\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`ExplainPlanAnalyzer.detectBottlenecks`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `detectBottlenecks(rootPlanNode)` to recursively inspect a plan tree and return structured diagnostic findings.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Traverse node and node.Plans; flag Seq Scan with rowsRemoved > actualRows * 5, Sort Method: external merge, or Q-Error >= 10.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 3\n\n### Step 4: Non-Sargable Predicate Rewriter\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Transforming Function-Wrapped Columns into Index-Range Predicates\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`ExplainPlanAnalyzer.rewriteSargable`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `rewriteSargable(predicateStr)` to transform `YEAR(col) = YYYY` and `col + k = v` into sargable range/equality predicates.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Rewrite YEAR(col) = YYYY to col >= \"YYYY-01-01\" AND col < \"(YYYY+1)-01-01\".`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 4\n\n## Relational & Storage Engine Guarantees\n\n- **Curriculum Domain**: Query Optimizer & Execution Plans\n- **Difficulty & Time Budget**: Advanced (~40 minutes)\n- **Key Architectural Highlights**:\n  - Cardinality estimation Q-Error = max(est/act, act/est) calculation across plan tree nodes\n  - Automated bottleneck flagging for Seq Scans with high Rows Removed by Filter and external disk Sorts\n  - Sargable SQL predicate rewriter transforming YEAR(col) = Y and arithmetic wrappers into indexable ranges\n- **Core Primitives & Tags**: `EXPLAIN ANALYZE`, `Cardinality Estimation`, `Q-Error`, `Sargability`, `Cost Model`\n\n## Related Curriculum Units\n\n- [life of a sql query pipeline](/topic/life-of-a-sql-query-pipeline/)\n- [reading explain and explain analyze](/topic/reading-explain-and-explain-analyze/)\n- [table statistics histograms cardinality](/topic/table-statistics-histograms-cardinality/)\n- [selectivity estimation correlated columns](/topic/selectivity-estimation-correlated-columns/)\n- [scan operators seq index bitmap](/topic/scan-operators-seq-index-bitmap/)\n\n## Production Database Context & Verification\n\nThis from-scratch relational engine component is engineered with zero external dependencies and deterministic verification harnesses. Every internal database invariant—from three-valued logic (`TRUE` / `FALSE` / `UNKNOWN`), referential integrity, and fan-out-free join pre-aggregation to B+Tree page splits, MVCC snapshot visibility (`xmin` / `xmax`), slotted-page compaction, and ARIES write-ahead log crash recovery—is asserted directly in `test.js`. Use the interactive browser workbench above to complete the 4 guided steps in **Guided Lab** mode or inspect and benchmark the complete reference architecture in **Full Solution** mode.\n"
