      "README.md": "# Implement & Benchmark Nested Loop, Hash Join & Sort-Merge Join\n\n## Architectural Overview\n\nA physical relational join engine implementing Block Nested Loop Join, in-memory Build-and-Probe Hash Join, Zipper Sort-Merge Join with duplicate peer rewind, and NULL-safe Hash Anti-Join.\n\nIn production relational and analytical database systems—spanning PostgreSQL, SQLite, MySQL/InnoDB, and DuckDB—understanding how query clauses, schema constraints, index structures, and storage engines execute under the hood separates surface-level query authors from staff-level database engineers. This capstone build lab guides you through implementing **Implement & Benchmark Nested Loop, Hash Join & Sort-Merge Join** from first principles with deterministic self-test invariants.\n\n## Guided Implementation Walkthrough (4 Progressive Steps)\n\n### Step 1: Block Nested Loop Join with Comparison Telemetry\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Evaluating Equi-Joins Across Outer and Inner Tuple Pairs\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`PhysicalJoinEngine.nestedLoopJoin`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `nestedLoopJoin(leftRows, rightRows, leftKey, rightKey)` returning `{ rows, comparisons }`, skipping `null`/`undefined` join keys per SQL `=` semantics.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Loop outer rows and inner rows; skip when either key is null/undefined; count comparisons.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 1\n\n### Step 2: Build-on-Smaller-Relation Hash Join\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: O(N + M) Hash Table Construction on the Smaller Input + Streaming Probe\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`PhysicalJoinEngine.hashJoin`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `hashJoin(leftRows, rightRows, leftKey, rightKey)` so that the smaller array is always selected as the hash build side, returning `{ rows, buildSize, probeOps }`.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Build a Map<key, Array<row>> on the smaller relation (ignoring null keys), then probe with the larger relation.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 2\n\n### Step 3: Zipper Sort-Merge Join with Duplicate Peer Group Rewind\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Advancing Two Sorted Streams in Lockstep and Taking the Cross-Product of Equal-Key Runs\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`PhysicalJoinEngine.sortMergeJoin`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `sortMergeJoin(leftRows, rightRows, leftKey, rightKey)` to sort both inputs on their join key and merge them in a single pass with peer-group expansion.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Sort both inputs by join key; when keys match, collect the contiguous run of equal keys on left and right and emit their Cartesian product.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 3\n\n### Step 4: NULL-Safe Hash Anti-Join\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: O(N + M) Anti-Join Execution Equivalence to NOT EXISTS\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`PhysicalJoinEngine.hashAntiJoin`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `hashAntiJoin(leftRows, rightRows, leftKey, rightKey)` to return all `leftRows` with no matching key in `rightRows`, safely ignoring `null` keys in `rightRows`.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Insert all non-null rightKeys into a Set, then keep leftRows whose leftKey is not in that Set.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 4\n\n## Relational & Storage Engine Guarantees\n\n- **Curriculum Domain**: Physical Join & Execution Operators\n- **Difficulty & Time Budget**: Advanced (~45 minutes)\n- **Key Architectural Highlights**:\n  - Block Nested Loop Join minimizing inner-relation scans via chunked outer buffering\n  - Build-on-smaller-input Hash Join achieving O(N + M) linear execution cost\n  - Sort-Merge Join with peer group mark-and-rewind for duplicate join keys\n- **Core Primitives & Tags**: `Hash Join`, `Sort-Merge Join`, `Nested Loop Join`, `Volcano Model`, `Physical Operators`\n\n## Related Curriculum Units\n\n- [nested loop join indexed nlj](/topic/nested-loop-join-indexed-nlj/)\n- [hash join build probe grace](/topic/hash-join-build-probe-grace/)\n- [sort merge join zipper mechanics](/topic/sort-merge-join-zipper-mechanics/)\n- [join order search dynamic programming](/topic/join-order-search-dynamic-programming/)\n- [predicate pushdown projection pruning](/topic/predicate-pushdown-projection-pruning/)\n\n## Production Database Context & Verification\n\nThis from-scratch relational engine component is engineered with zero external dependencies and deterministic verification harnesses. Every internal database invariant—from three-valued logic (`TRUE` / `FALSE` / `UNKNOWN`), referential integrity, and fan-out-free join pre-aggregation to B+Tree page splits, MVCC snapshot visibility (`xmin` / `xmax`), slotted-page compaction, and ARIES write-ahead log crash recovery—is asserted directly in `test.js`. Use the interactive browser workbench above to complete the 4 guided steps in **Guided Lab** mode or inspect and benchmark the complete reference architecture in **Full Solution** mode.\n"
