      "README.md": "# 8KB Slotted Page + Write-Ahead Log Crash Recovery Simulator\n\n## Architectural Overview\n\nA disk-page storage engine implementing an 8KB slotted page with downward line-pointer array growth and upward tuple growth, PageLSN tracking, and 3-phase ARIES crash recovery (Analysis, Redo, Undo).\n\nIn production relational and analytical database systems—spanning PostgreSQL, SQLite, MySQL/InnoDB, and DuckDB—understanding how query clauses, schema constraints, index structures, and storage engines execute under the hood separates surface-level query authors from staff-level database engineers. This capstone build lab guides you through implementing **8KB Slotted Page + Write-Ahead Log Crash Recovery Simulator** from first principles with deterministic self-test invariants.\n\n## Guided Implementation Walkthrough (4 Progressive Steps)\n\n### Step 1: 8KB Slotted Page Tuple Allocation (pd_lower & pd_upper)\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Growing Line Pointer Slots Downward From Header and Tuple Payloads Upward From Page End\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`SlottedPageWalEngine.insertTuple`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `insertTuple(payloadStr, lsn)` to allocate space in an 8192-byte slotted page where header `pd_lower` grows downward by 4 bytes per slot and `pd_upper` grows upward by tuple byte length.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Check freeSpace >= 4 + byteLength; allocate tuple at pd_upper - len, append slot { offset, length, dead: false }, and advance pd_lower += 4.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 1\n\n### Step 2: Tuple Deletion & In-Place Page Compaction\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Defragmenting Dead Tuple Holes While Preserving External Slot Numbers (TIDs)\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`SlottedPageWalEngine.compactPage`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `deleteTuple(slotId, lsn)` and `compactPage()` so that dead tuple bytes are reclaimed and `pd_upper` is restored while every live tuple keeps its original `slotId`.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Repack all live tuples contiguously from pageSize downward, updating each live slot’s offset without changing its slot index.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 2\n\n### Step 3: ARIES WAL Analysis Phase (Active Tx Table & Dirty Page Table)\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Reconstructing Loser Transactions and Redo Start LSN from the Write-Ahead Log\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`SlottedPageWalEngine.analyzeWal`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `analyzeWal(walRecords)` to identify uncommitted `loserTxs` and the minimum `redoStartLsn` across dirty pages.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Scan WAL forward: track active/loser transactions on BEGIN/UPDATE/COMMIT, and record first recLSN per page in dirtyPages.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 3\n\n### Step 4: ARIES Redo (Repeating History) & Undo (Loser Rollback)\n\n- **Core Database Concept**: Applying Logged Changes Where pageLSN < record.lsn and Rolling Back Losers in Reverse LSN Order\n- **Target Module**: `index.js` (`SlottedPageWalEngine.recoverWal`)\n- **Engineering Specification**: Implement `recoverWal(walRecords, initialPages)` to execute ARIES Redo followed by reverse-LSN Undo of uncommitted loser transactions.\n- **Implementation Hint**: `Redo all UPDATE records forward to reconstruct state at crash, then walk loserTx UPDATE records in reverse LSN order restoring beforeImage.`\n- **Verification Invariant**: deterministic assertion verified in `test.js` step 4\n\n## Relational & Storage Engine Guarantees\n\n- **Curriculum Domain**: Storage Engines, Buffer Pool & WAL\n- **Difficulty & Time Budget**: Advanced (~45 minutes)\n- **Key Architectural Highlights**:\n  - 8KB Slotted Page memory layout growing line pointers downward and variable-length tuples upward\n  - In-place line-pointer compaction reclaiming fragmented tuple space without changing external TIDs\n  - Three-phase ARIES WAL recovery (Analysis, Redo from minRecLSN, and reverse Undo with CLR logging)\n- **Core Primitives & Tags**: `Slotted Page`, `Write-Ahead Logging`, `ARIES Recovery`, `PageLSN`, `Buffer Pool`\n\n## Related Curriculum Units\n\n- [slotted page layout 8kb anatomy](/topic/slotted-page-layout-8kb-anatomy/)\n- [heap files hot updates fillfactor](/topic/heap-files-hot-updates-fillfactor/)\n- [buffer pool clock sweep lru k](/topic/buffer-pool-clock-sweep-lru-k/)\n- [write ahead logging wal lsn](/topic/write-ahead-logging-wal-lsn/)\n- [checkpoints dirty page flushing](/topic/checkpoints-dirty-page-flushing/)\n\n## Production Database Context & Verification\n\nThis from-scratch relational engine component is engineered with zero external dependencies and deterministic verification harnesses. Every internal database invariant—from three-valued logic (`TRUE` / `FALSE` / `UNKNOWN`), referential integrity, and fan-out-free join pre-aggregation to B+Tree page splits, MVCC snapshot visibility (`xmin` / `xmax`), slotted-page compaction, and ARIES write-ahead log crash recovery—is asserted directly in `test.js`. Use the interactive browser workbench above to complete the 4 guided steps in **Guided Lab** mode or inspect and benchmark the complete reference architecture in **Full Solution** mode.\n"
